{
  "$comment": "EDE-105 (approved on EDE-94): THE CHAT STORE, one Rust crate for every client (apps/desktop/crates/chat-store: a pure core + a SQLite adapter, no async runtime in the core) that keeps every chat on every device, offline, opened from disk, plus a local search index. This TS reference (src/chat-store.ts) and the crate (its in-memory core AND its SQLite adapter) replay every case below. WHAT IT HOLDS, per account (desktop: `{data_dir}/accounts/<account>/chat-store.sqlite`, beside the sync store, kept across sign-out like it, gone with the account's data): (1) the synced `messages` rows of every chat the member can see (the `messages` shape's own visibility rule), OPENED with the chat key (EXP-1459, `sealed-content.json`); a row whose key is not held yet is stored with `body: null`, never indexed, and replaced (latest wins, by id) once the key arrives and it opens; (2) the TRANSCRIPT EVENTS of every session of those chats (the wire `activity` events with their seq, exactly as on the wire: already scrubbed by the emitter, never more than a viewer sees), with `rootId`, `sessionId`, `seq` and `storedAt` (ms the store took it). TRANSCRIPTS NEVER TOUCH THE SERVER: events reach a store only from the device running the session or another reader device, over eNet (steer-enet.json); the server keeps carrying the messages only. DECRYPTED ONLY WHERE THE PLATFORM STORE IS PROTECTED: desktop = the per-account data dir, user-only (0600 file, like the journal and the keyring); iOS = Data Protection (complete until first unlock) in the app container; Android = app-private storage; web = OPFS (origin-private). A platform without a protected store keeps the bodies sealed as synced and indexes nothing sealed. DEDUP: an event is keyed by (sessionId, seq): the first write wins, a repeat (a history page overlapping the live feed, a second reader answering the same page) is dropped; events read back per session in seq order (`ingest.cases`). INDEX SCOPE (`docs`): user inputs (`user_message`), narration, tool titles (`name` + ` ` + `detail`, or `name`), tool output as on the wire (`tool_update` `output`, else its `diff`; the hit lands on the tool's row: the lowest seq of a `tool` with that id in the session, else the update's own seq) and synced message bodies (`message`); NEVER thoughts, never slots (usage, config, diff snapshots) or card payloads. A doc's time = the event's `at`, else `storedAt` (a message: `createdAt`). QUERY SEMANTICS = steer-enet.json SEARCH (find in chat, EDE-96): a case- and diacritics-insensitive LITERAL: the query and the text collapse every run of ASCII whitespace to one space (trimmed), fold per code point (NFD, marks dropped, lowercased), the query keeps its first `queryMaxChars` code points, an empty query searches nothing; one hit per doc (its first match), `snippet` = the collapsed text from `snippetLeadChars` before the match, `snippetChars` wide (more only for a longer match), `…` where cut, `matchStart`/`matchLen` in code points of the snippet. DEDUP OF HITS: a `message` hit whose collapsed body equals a `user_message`/`narration` hit's text in the same session is dropped (the final reply and the person's input exist twice; the transcript row is the one a reader lands on). ORDER: newest first by time, then session id ascending, then seq descending (a message, without a seq, after the events of the same instant), then message id. FIND IN CHAT (`search.chatCases`): one chat (`rootId`, every session of its tree), at most `limit` hits (clamped to [1, hitsMax]), `total` = every hit. GLOBAL (`search.allCases`, S5): one row per chat {rootId, count, hit = its newest hit}, newest chat first, at most `limit` rows, `total` = chats matched. OPEN: a chat opens from the store before any live feed attaches: per session, its stored events through the same REPLAY TAIL rule a join replays by (steer-enet.json), older ones paged from the store; the live feed's `activity_reset` replay then replaces the seed and everything it carries is stored as it arrives. RETENTION (`retention`): per form factor (`constants.retentionDays`): desktop keeps everything (null); phones and web keep prose (inputs, narration) and every synced message forever and every other event (tool steps, their output, slots) for the last `retentionDays` days by its time (the cutoff instant kept); a storage setting changes the window; an older tool step is fetched over eNet when its chat is opened (S2). PHASES: S1 = this spec + the crate + desktop (the store fed from the device's own journals, the synced messages and every feed the desktop views; a chat opens from it). S2 = background catch-up over eNet: a reader asks the running device or ANY reader device holding the events (its store answers `history_page` and the EDE-96 `search` frame like a journal does) for the seqs it lacks below and above its span, deduped by seq. S3 = phones through `exponential-mobile-ffi` (the same crate; iOS + Android retention 30 days). S4 = web through wasm with the store in OPFS. S5 = the Chats section in global search (EDE-99) reading `searchAll`.",
  "constants": {
    "queryMaxChars": 200,
    "hitsMax": 50,
    "snippetChars": 120,
    "snippetLeadChars": 40,
    "retentionDays": {
      "desktop": null,
      "phone": 30,
      "web": 30
    }
  },
